1
00:00:02,830 --> 00:00:06,006
-♪ In the not-too-distant
future ♪

2
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:09,112
♪ Somewhere
in time and space ♪

3
00:00:09,147 --> 00:00:12,253
♪ Mike Nelson
and his robot pals ♪

4
00:00:12,288 --> 00:00:15,360
♪ Are caught
in an endless chase ♪

5
00:00:15,394 --> 00:00:18,501
♪ Pursued by a woman
whose name is Pearl ♪

6
00:00:18,535 --> 00:00:21,538
♪ An evil gal who wants
to rule the world ♪

7
00:00:21,573 --> 00:00:24,369
♪ She threw a few things
in her purse ♪

8
00:00:24,403 --> 00:00:26,129
♪ And in her rocket ship,
she hunts him ♪

9
00:00:26,164 --> 00:00:28,338
♪ All across the universe

10
00:00:28,373 --> 00:00:30,892
-I'll get you!

11
00:00:30,927 --> 00:00:34,034
♪ I'll send him
cheesy movies ♪

12
00:00:34,068 --> 00:00:36,070
♪ The worst I can find

13
00:00:36,105 --> 00:00:37,278
♪ La, la, la

14
00:00:37,313 --> 00:00:39,970
♪ He'll have to sit
and watch them all ♪

15
00:00:40,005 --> 00:00:42,180
♪ And I'll monitor his mind

16
00:00:42,214 --> 00:00:43,457
-♪ La, la, la

17
00:00:43,491 --> 00:00:46,253
-♪ Now keep in mind
Mike can't control ♪

18
00:00:46,287 --> 00:00:48,669
♪ Where the movies
begin or end ♪

19
00:00:48,703 --> 00:00:49,808
-♪ La, la, la

20
00:00:49,842 --> 00:00:52,431
-♪ He'll try to keep
his sanity ♪

21
00:00:52,466 --> 00:00:57,402
♪ With the help
of his robot friends ♪

22
00:00:57,436 --> 00:00:59,093
-Robot roll call.

23
00:00:59,128 --> 00:01:00,715
Cambot!
-You're on.

24
00:01:00,750 --> 00:01:01,854
-Gypsy!
-Oh, my stars!

25
00:01:01,889 --> 00:01:03,891
-Tom Servo!
-Check me out.

26
00:01:03,925 --> 00:01:05,582
-Crow!
-I'm different!

27
00:01:05,617 --> 00:01:08,378
-♪ If you're wondering
how he eats and breathes ♪

28
00:01:08,413 --> 00:01:11,312
♪ And other science facts 
-♪ La la la

29
00:01:11,347 --> 00:01:14,315
-♪ Just repeat to yourself,
"It's just a show" ♪

30
00:01:14,350 --> 00:01:17,732
♪ "I should really just relax"

31
00:01:17,767 --> 00:01:22,841
For "Mystery Science
Theater 3000."

32
00:01:22,875 --> 00:01:25,223
♪♪

33
00:01:36,682 --> 00:01:37,649
-Hi, everyone.

34
00:01:37,683 --> 00:01:39,340
Welcome to
The Satellite of Love.

35
00:01:39,375 --> 00:01:42,723
My name is Mike Nelson...
or it used to be.

36
00:01:42,757 --> 00:01:45,588
You see, until recently,
I was just like you.

37
00:01:45,622 --> 00:01:47,728
I believed that everything
that was taught me was right,

38
00:01:47,762 --> 00:01:49,902
and everything was as it seemed,

39
00:01:49,937 --> 00:01:52,284
and then one day,I found myself pursued by agents

40
00:01:52,319 --> 00:01:55,494
of a secret government project
who basically wiped out

41
00:01:55,529 --> 00:01:58,566
every shred of evidence
that I ever existed.

42
00:01:58,601 --> 00:02:03,261
They took everything --
my identity, my life.

43
00:02:03,295 --> 00:02:05,401
Now I'm on the run, never
knowing when I'll be caught

44
00:02:05,435 --> 00:02:07,886
or where my enemies
will turn up,

45
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:11,338
but they should know...
I will do anything

46
00:02:11,372 --> 00:02:12,925
to get back what is mine.

47
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:14,789
-Hey, Mike! Mike!
-Yeah?

48
00:02:14,824 --> 00:02:16,343
-We found your wallet.
It was in your room.

49
00:02:16,377 --> 00:02:17,620
-Oh. [Chuckles]

50
00:02:17,654 --> 00:02:18,931
-Yeah, everything about
your identity is there.

51
00:02:18,966 --> 00:02:20,761
You can relax.
-Ugh! I guess I didn't have to

52
00:02:20,795 --> 00:02:22,763
do very much at all
to get back what's mine.

53
00:02:22,797 --> 00:02:24,074
-Nope.
-You weren't telling them about

54
00:02:24,109 --> 00:02:26,111
the secret government
conspiracy, were you?

55
00:02:26,146 --> 00:02:27,664
-Well, my wallet was missing.

56
00:02:27,699 --> 00:02:30,046
-Folks, listen --
Pay no attention to this guy.

57
00:02:30,080 --> 00:02:32,324
Everything is exactly
as it seems.

58
00:02:32,359 --> 00:02:34,775
-We'll be right back.
Wait a minute. Wait a minute.

59
00:02:34,809 --> 00:02:36,777
How do I know
this wallet is mine?

60
00:02:36,811 --> 00:02:39,055
-It is. Look -- same picture
of Mark Spitz, even.

61
00:02:39,089 --> 00:02:41,816
-Oh, good.
-It's sad, really.

62
00:02:41,851 --> 00:02:47,236
♪♪

63
00:02:49,134 --> 00:02:51,619
-Whew. Got to say, it's good
to have the ol' identity ba--

64
00:02:51,654 --> 00:02:53,069
Aah!
-What?! What?!

65
00:02:53,103 --> 00:02:54,898
-What?! Mike!
-They took my identity!

66
00:02:54,933 --> 00:02:57,211
Everything I ever -- Oh, wait.
It's right here. Sorry.

67
00:02:57,246 --> 00:02:58,833
-Oh. Ms. Forrester is calling.

68
00:02:58,868 --> 00:03:01,526
-And you want to hang onto
an identity like that, huh?

69
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:03,355
Sheesh.

70
00:03:03,390 --> 00:03:05,840
-Aloha! Welcome aboard!

71
00:03:05,875 --> 00:03:07,704
Welcome!
-Aloha!

72
00:03:07,739 --> 00:03:08,912
-Bobo. Bobo, I think the idea

73
00:03:08,947 --> 00:03:10,638
is to distribute them
one by one,

74
00:03:10,673 --> 00:03:12,709
and then let the guests
handle it from there.

75
00:03:12,744 --> 00:03:14,918
-[Laughs] I get it.
How silly of me.

76
00:03:14,953 --> 00:03:16,955
-Hello! Aloha!

77
00:03:16,989 --> 00:03:19,716
-Idiot!
Let me show you to your cabin.

78
00:03:19,751 --> 00:03:22,478
-Bon voyage! Arrivederci
-Ow! Ow!

79
00:03:22,512 --> 00:03:24,204
-Son of Nel, listen.

80
00:03:24,238 --> 00:03:26,758
Our phone number accidentally
got printed in an ad

81
00:03:26,792 --> 00:03:28,242
for a cruise-ship deal.

82
00:03:28,277 --> 00:03:32,557
Bobo took 2,500 reservations
before he told me,

83
00:03:32,591 --> 00:03:36,008
but the money's so sweet,
I decided to keep it.

84
00:03:36,043 --> 00:03:38,563
Then we left port
before they could get on.

85
00:03:38,597 --> 00:03:40,565
[Chuckles]

86
00:03:40,599 --> 00:03:42,601
Well, except for those
two early nerds.

87
00:03:42,636 --> 00:03:48,745
But [chuckles]
we left 2,498 suckers ashore!

88
00:03:48,780 --> 00:03:51,748
[Chuckles]

89
00:03:51,783 --> 00:03:53,923
[All chuckling nervously]

90
00:03:53,957 --> 00:03:56,063
But you live
in a castle, so...?

91
00:03:56,097 --> 00:03:58,514
[All continue
chuckling nervously]

92
00:03:58,548 --> 00:04:02,034
-Shut up. Okay, we got to give
them the whole QE2 deal,

93
00:04:02,069 --> 00:04:04,796
so we need ice sculptures
for the buffet table.

94
00:04:04,830 --> 00:04:07,350
Hey. Hey, Clorox-face.
Send him the raw materials.

95
00:04:07,385 --> 00:04:09,110
-Aye, aye, sir!

96
00:04:09,145 --> 00:04:12,148
-Shut up, and just do it.
-Right.

97
00:04:12,182 --> 00:04:13,563
[Warbling]

98
00:04:13,598 --> 00:04:14,392
Boy.

99
00:04:14,426 --> 00:04:16,048
[Pop!]

100
00:04:16,083 --> 00:04:16,704
-Ugh.
-Wa-huh?

101
00:04:16,739 --> 00:04:19,017
-Huh.

102
00:04:19,051 --> 00:04:20,881
Huh.

103
00:04:20,915 --> 00:04:22,952
-Anna and I would like to see
the upper deck now.

104
00:04:22,986 --> 00:04:24,264
-Oh, sure, but --

105
00:04:24,298 --> 00:04:26,645
Oh, the seas
are too rough right now!

106
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:28,060
Whoa! Feel that?

107
00:04:28,095 --> 00:04:30,822
-Oh! Too rough
to feed you, even.

108
00:04:30,856 --> 00:04:33,480
-But still, uh,
smell that salt air.

109
00:04:33,514 --> 00:04:36,552
-Ow.
-I'm getting sick, Norm.

110
00:04:36,586 --> 00:04:38,588
-Mrs. Dash air, actually.

111
00:04:38,623 --> 00:04:41,281
-Hey, lawgiver, it's not too
rough to feed me, is it?

112
00:04:41,315 --> 00:04:43,213
I mean, it's not
too rough to -- Yeow!

113
00:04:43,248 --> 00:04:44,905
-Okay, let's see what you got.

114
00:04:44,939 --> 00:04:47,770
-Well, now, I made a sort of
environmental sculpture

115
00:04:47,804 --> 00:04:49,806
with my ice,
setting it in a surrounding

116
00:04:49,841 --> 00:04:51,394
of gin and tonic,

117
00:04:51,429 --> 00:04:54,052
aesthetically pleasing
and very, very refreshing.

118
00:04:54,086 --> 00:04:55,329
[Chuckles]

119
00:04:55,364 --> 00:05:01,577
-I, uh -- I tried
to weld mine, and, uh...

120
00:05:01,611 --> 00:05:04,027
-Yeah, you did.
-Yeah.

121
00:05:04,062 --> 00:05:06,029
-I don't know.

122
00:05:06,064 --> 00:05:09,930
-Well, I give you,
Michelangelo's "David."

123
00:05:09,964 --> 00:05:11,759
-Wow, Crow,
bigger than the original

124
00:05:11,794 --> 00:05:12,933
and out of four ice cubes?

125
00:05:12,967 --> 00:05:14,244
-Ah, I'm just efficient,
I guess.

126
00:05:14,279 --> 00:05:16,419
-Man.
-Yeah, I could've, uh --

127
00:05:16,454 --> 00:05:18,145
could've done that,
I guess, but I --

128
00:05:18,179 --> 00:05:21,010
I was, uh,
trying to weld mine, and...

129
00:05:21,044 --> 00:05:23,978
-Right, Mike,
you made that clear.

130
00:05:24,013 --> 00:05:26,567
-And now it's time
for your on-deck movie

131
00:05:26,602 --> 00:05:28,120
to be held below decks today

132
00:05:28,155 --> 00:05:30,951
because of the aforementioned
rough seas.

133
00:05:30,985 --> 00:05:32,746
[All shouting]

134
00:05:32,780 --> 00:05:34,230
-It's called "Devil Fish,"

135
00:05:34,264 --> 00:05:36,025
and it features
many nautical themes

136
00:05:36,059 --> 00:05:38,683
and many Italians pretending
to be Floridians.

137
00:05:38,717 --> 00:05:40,547
-[Crying]
-Mike and Bots, also enjoy.

138
00:05:40,581 --> 00:05:42,065
Brain Pan, send it.
-Yeah.

139
00:05:42,100 --> 00:05:46,656
[Warbling]

140
00:05:46,691 --> 00:05:48,796
-He just needs
a little off the calf.

141
00:05:48,831 --> 00:05:51,316
-No, stop it!
Good gravy, man!

142
00:05:51,351 --> 00:05:52,973
Don't you ever learn?
-Sorry.

143
00:05:53,007 --> 00:05:54,871
[Buzzer]
Oh, we got movie sign!

144
00:06:08,437 --> 00:06:11,543
-Sorry.
-It's okay.

145
00:06:11,578 --> 00:06:16,548
-Hey, Bebe Rebozo's home movies.

146
00:06:16,583 --> 00:06:19,931
-I told her, you know, and I
told her, loudly and clearly.

147
00:06:19,965 --> 00:06:23,003
-Yes, dear. Yes, dear.

148
00:06:23,037 --> 00:06:24,314
-Them doing it, dear.
Yes, dear.

149
00:06:24,349 --> 00:06:26,144
-Who was it that said,
"I never met a kid I liked."

150
00:06:26,178 --> 00:06:27,387
W.C. Fields, I think.

151
00:06:27,421 --> 00:06:28,733
Well, that's the way
I feel about it...

152
00:06:28,767 --> 00:06:30,010
-Yes, dear.
-...when they're on my boat.

153
00:06:30,044 --> 00:06:33,151
-Oh, I mean our boat.

154
00:06:33,185 --> 00:06:37,086
-"2000 Flushes: The Movie."

155
00:06:37,120 --> 00:06:42,263
♪♪

156
00:06:42,298 --> 00:06:45,750
-Something vague
this way comes.

157
00:06:45,784 --> 00:06:48,649
-Cole, are you listening to me?
-Yeah, Molly, I'm listening.

158
00:06:48,684 --> 00:06:50,271
-Mostly, I'm eating.

159
00:06:50,306 --> 00:06:53,482
♪♪

160
00:06:53,516 --> 00:06:54,759
-You know what she had
the nerve to say?

161
00:06:54,793 --> 00:06:56,208
You know what she said?

162
00:06:56,243 --> 00:06:58,763
-What she said, after this.
-Ow!

163
00:06:58,797 --> 00:07:01,317
-Oh, Cole, did you
cut yourself?

164
00:07:01,351 --> 00:07:03,146
-Oh, relax.
I mean, it's just a scratch.

165
00:07:03,181 --> 00:07:05,252
-And you could get infected!
I'll go get the iodine.

166
00:07:05,286 --> 00:07:08,358
-Ooh.
-It's Gertrude Stein.

167
00:07:08,393 --> 00:07:11,016
♪♪

168
00:07:11,051 --> 00:07:12,604
-[Imitating music]

169
00:07:12,639 --> 00:07:15,745
-Well, I can eat the boat
and spit them out, I suppose.

170
00:07:15,780 --> 00:07:18,023
♪♪

171
00:07:18,058 --> 00:07:21,164
-We now return
to "The Cut Finger Story."

172
00:07:21,199 --> 00:07:27,377
♪♪

173
00:07:27,412 --> 00:07:28,896
-Man, it's farther up
than I thought.

174
00:07:28,931 --> 00:07:30,346
This is taking forever!

175
00:07:30,380 --> 00:07:35,316
♪♪

176
00:07:35,351 --> 00:07:39,251
[Both screaming]
-Aah! Save the Metamucil!

177
00:07:39,286 --> 00:07:42,289
-Film crew is really having fun
throwing stuff at her.

178
00:07:42,323 --> 00:07:44,084
-[Chuckles]

179
00:07:44,118 --> 00:07:48,502
-Cole! Cole!
-Caw! Caw!

180
00:07:48,537 --> 00:07:52,161
-I guess he didn't like
the pork tartare.

181
00:07:58,892 --> 00:07:59,927
-Cole?

182
00:07:59,962 --> 00:08:03,586
-Mrs. Kilroy was here.
-Darling?

183
00:08:03,621 --> 00:08:06,934
-Let me clear the table off
for you, ma'am! Thanks.

184
00:08:06,969 --> 00:08:08,729
-Our special tonight
is devil fish

185
00:08:08,764 --> 00:08:13,113
with satanic string beans
and deep lucifered potatoes.

186
00:08:13,147 --> 00:08:15,149
-[Screaming]

187
00:08:15,184 --> 00:08:17,531
-This fish has a lot of nerve!

188
00:08:17,566 --> 00:08:20,361
♪♪

189
00:08:20,396 --> 00:08:21,708
-Ooh.

190
00:08:21,742 --> 00:08:26,471
-Yeah, we got dolphins
in the basement.

191
00:08:26,506 --> 00:08:32,512
-No. Wrong.
Do it again.

192
00:08:32,546 --> 00:08:36,757
-♪ This is the dawning
of the age of Seaquarium ♪

193
00:08:36,792 --> 00:08:38,897
[Dolphins squeaking]

194
00:08:38,932 --> 00:08:40,623
-Peter Frampton!

195
00:08:40,658 --> 00:08:43,212
♪♪

196
00:08:43,246 --> 00:08:44,558
-What?

197
00:08:44,593 --> 00:08:47,285
Man, the Staten Island ferry
is way off course.

198
00:08:47,319 --> 00:08:51,151
-[Imitating music]

199
00:08:51,185 --> 00:08:53,878
-No, don't put me in there!
There's sharks in there!

200
00:08:53,912 --> 00:08:56,087
Oh, wait.

201
00:08:56,121 --> 00:09:00,712
-[Imitating music]

202
00:09:00,747 --> 00:09:03,991
-Hey, temp workers!
-D'oh.

203
00:09:04,026 --> 00:09:06,822
-I am pleased at things.

204
00:09:06,856 --> 00:09:08,755
-No, no, I'm not going
to fall for that.

205
00:09:08,789 --> 00:09:11,965
-No, really, I am getting
divorced, toots!

206
00:09:11,999 --> 00:09:13,587
-I love you.

207
00:09:13,622 --> 00:09:16,728
♪♪

208
00:09:16,763 --> 00:09:19,800
-Hey, fish, now!
-Hey, you haven't thanked me.

209
00:09:19,835 --> 00:09:22,113
Come here, Donald! Come on.

210
00:09:22,147 --> 00:09:26,324
-Hey, don't call me Donald.My name is [imitates squeaking]!

211
00:09:26,358 --> 00:09:30,017
-Aww.
-Shush up.

212
00:09:30,052 --> 00:09:32,606
-Now, how would you rate
that fish?

213
00:09:32,641 --> 00:09:34,297
-You've had enough.
-Ugh!

214
00:09:34,332 --> 00:09:37,059
What did you put in that fish?!
[Imitates choking]

215
00:09:37,093 --> 00:09:40,476
-You're a fatty!

216
00:09:40,510 --> 00:09:43,272
-Now that concludes
our tour inside.

217
00:09:43,306 --> 00:09:46,171
Outside, the outdoor pool,
where the dolphins are together

218
00:09:46,206 --> 00:09:48,622
with researcher Stella Dickens,
their trainer.

219
00:09:48,657 --> 00:09:50,866
This way.

220
00:09:50,900 --> 00:09:53,109
-Isn't that something?
-It can move.

221
00:09:53,144 --> 00:09:54,663
-What do you do, exactly?

222
00:09:54,697 --> 00:09:57,217
-I study their behavior here
in captivity

223
00:09:57,251 --> 00:09:59,668
and also
in their natural habitat,

224
00:09:59,702 --> 00:10:01,255
and right now, Dr. Bob Hogan,

225
00:10:01,290 --> 00:10:04,604
my associate, is at sea
conducting an experiment.

226
00:10:04,638 --> 00:10:07,814
-Dr. Bob Hogan is alsoexperimenting with film credits.

227
00:10:07,848 --> 00:10:10,506
♪♪

228
00:10:10,540 --> 00:10:15,580
-"Devil Fish," the story
of Aleister Crappie.

229
00:10:15,615 --> 00:10:16,857
-Oof.
-Hey, look, they spelled

230
00:10:16,892 --> 00:10:20,136
his name sideways!

231
00:10:20,171 --> 00:10:23,277
-It's a man wearing
a London phone booth!

232
00:10:23,312 --> 00:10:25,348
-Ooh, turtle.

233
00:10:25,383 --> 00:10:28,351
-So, Mike, turtles excrete wax,
and you humans put it in cans

234
00:10:28,386 --> 00:10:30,043
and just rub it
all over your cars?

235
00:10:30,077 --> 00:10:33,046
Good. That's good.
Just keep doing that.

236
00:10:33,080 --> 00:10:35,669
-It's not exactly how it goes.

237
00:10:35,704 --> 00:10:38,914
♪♪

238
00:10:38,948 --> 00:10:40,294
-Say, uh, whose fish is this?

239
00:10:40,329 --> 00:10:42,124
Somebody lose this fish?

240
00:10:42,158 --> 00:10:45,472
♪♪

241
00:10:45,506 --> 00:10:48,026
-Man, feeding
the whole ocean is hard!

242
00:10:48,061 --> 00:10:49,856
♪♪

243
00:10:49,890 --> 00:10:54,584
-♪ Don't say
things you're gonna ♪

244
00:10:54,619 --> 00:10:56,310
-"General organizer" --

245
00:10:56,345 --> 00:10:58,485
Just put some things over there
and over there.

246
00:10:58,519 --> 00:11:03,041
♪♪

247
00:11:03,076 --> 00:11:04,733
-They're going to airlift us
out of the movie!

248
00:11:04,767 --> 00:11:05,734
Here we are!
-Right here!

249
00:11:05,768 --> 00:11:08,115
-Here we are!
-Here!

250
00:11:08,150 --> 00:11:09,703
