eye color gross?

748
00:33:28,765 --> 00:33:31,975
-When will he be ready?
-Oh, just a couple more hours.

749
00:33:34,184 --> 00:33:36,911
-I'm going back to Italy. Bye.

750
00:33:36,945 --> 00:33:40,846
♪♪

751
00:33:40,880 --> 00:33:43,952
-Eh, kiss my ink sack.

752
00:33:46,472 --> 00:33:50,683
-[Vocalizing "Sailor's
Hornpipe"] Crap.

753
00:33:50,718 --> 00:33:53,514
-I'm sorry about your vacation.

754
00:33:53,548 --> 00:33:55,102
-Really?
-Oh, no.

755
00:33:55,136 --> 00:33:59,727
He suspects my insincerity
about his vacation.

756
00:33:59,761 --> 00:34:01,660
-So far, I like
these scenes the best.

757
00:34:01,694 --> 00:34:05,595
♪♪

758
00:34:05,629 --> 00:34:08,046
-I was going to say how sorry
I was about your cat dying,

759
00:34:08,080 --> 00:34:09,633
but forget it.

760
00:34:09,668 --> 00:34:12,395
♪♪

761
00:34:12,429 --> 00:34:14,328
-Oh, I forgot to lick the beer
off the can.

762
00:34:14,362 --> 00:34:17,641
[Warbling]

763
00:34:17,676 --> 00:34:18,918
-What's that?
-Kraftwerk.

764
00:34:18,953 --> 00:34:20,679
-I'm not sure.

765
00:34:20,713 --> 00:34:23,268
Hang on a second.

766
00:34:23,302 --> 00:34:25,787
Wait.
-Hold on. Wait. Pause.

767
00:34:25,822 --> 00:34:26,961
-Okay, we got it.

768
00:34:26,995 --> 00:34:30,206
-A shark?
-You think it's him?

769
00:34:30,240 --> 00:34:33,588
-I don't know.
Might be. It's moving fast.

770
00:34:33,623 --> 00:34:36,246
Almost 30 knots.

771
00:34:36,281 --> 00:34:38,904
Judging from the sound
of its echo,

772
00:34:38,938 --> 00:34:41,596
displaces a tremendous
amount of water for a fish.

773
00:34:41,631 --> 00:34:45,704
-Did you read anything else?

774
00:34:45,738 --> 00:34:48,120
-I don't know.
It must have dived too deep.

775
00:34:48,155 --> 00:34:51,227
-Pity.
-Yeah, to say the least.

776
00:34:51,261 --> 00:34:53,505
-Maybe it wasn't him.

777
00:34:53,539 --> 00:34:55,472
Hey, Bob, save us a beer,
too, huh.

778
00:34:55,507 --> 00:34:57,267
-I was framed, I tell you.
-You want a beer?

779
00:34:57,302 --> 00:35:00,788
Then find that fish.
-That's Euro funny.

780
00:35:00,822 --> 00:35:05,482
♪♪

781
00:35:05,517 --> 00:35:07,898
-Well, how do these fit?

782
00:35:07,933 --> 00:35:11,109
-You did a good job.
-Buy yourself something ugly.

783
00:35:11,143 --> 00:35:13,904
-Need anything else?
-Just keep an eye on him.

784
00:35:13,939 --> 00:35:16,942
I'll let you know when
we need something else.

785
00:35:23,293 --> 00:35:25,261
-Oh.

786
00:35:25,295 --> 00:35:29,196
-Man, Jet Skis
are getting huge.

787
00:35:29,230 --> 00:35:32,475
-I was only 19 when I met Bob.
-That's when I was skinny.

788
00:35:32,509 --> 00:35:34,408
-He was with the English
Oceanic Institute

789
00:35:34,442 --> 00:35:36,651
before coming to Florida.

790
00:35:36,686 --> 00:35:38,653
I liked working
with him immediately.

791
00:35:38,688 --> 00:35:41,311
-Cello -- 12 fathoms.

792
00:35:41,346 --> 00:35:43,210
-Okay, it's him!

793
00:35:43,244 --> 00:35:45,936
Peter!

794
00:35:45,971 --> 00:35:48,180
-Wow!
-Oh, incoming.

795
00:35:48,215 --> 00:35:50,217
♪♪

796
00:35:50,251 --> 00:35:51,942
[Warbling]

797
00:35:51,977 --> 00:35:55,739
-I hung one out for fun.
[Chuckles]

798
00:35:55,774 --> 00:35:56,913
-I think it's that thing
that comes out

799
00:35:56,947 --> 00:35:58,259
of the Wizard of Id's cauldron.

800
00:35:58,294 --> 00:35:59,743
-Oh, yeah.

801
00:35:59,778 --> 00:36:02,090
[Garbling]

802
00:36:02,125 --> 00:36:04,955
-It's his sound.
It's him!

803
00:36:07,889 --> 00:36:09,891
-What do I think?

804
00:36:09,926 --> 00:36:11,824
-Come on, baby.

805
00:36:11,859 --> 00:36:14,413
Come on up.

806
00:36:14,448 --> 00:36:17,209
-[Imitates static]
♪ Slow ride

807
00:36:17,244 --> 00:36:19,038
-Well, we got 3 hours
before it gets here.

808
00:36:19,073 --> 00:36:20,833
Want to play Risk?

809
00:36:20,868 --> 00:36:22,973
-Let's see if he records.

810
00:36:23,008 --> 00:36:27,530
-♪ I dream of genie

811
00:36:27,564 --> 00:36:32,569
-You bloody, rotten,
filthy sob, let me hear you!

812
00:36:32,604 --> 00:36:35,745
-Well, I'm glub I guess.

813
00:36:35,779 --> 00:36:38,126
-It's bearing one, two, zero,

814
00:36:38,161 --> 00:36:41,302
coming up at us two points
off the starboard bow.

815
00:36:41,337 --> 00:36:43,856
-How big is it?
-I don't know yet.

816
00:36:43,891 --> 00:36:45,927
-You think it will record?

817
00:36:45,962 --> 00:36:47,653
-Well, let's hope so.

818
00:36:47,688 --> 00:36:50,138
-Although we are having 
tentacledifficulties.

819
00:36:50,173 --> 00:36:51,899
-These will filter out
all the interference.

820
00:36:51,933 --> 00:36:55,937
Once I lock onto his frequency,
it will be computerized.

821
00:36:55,972 --> 00:36:59,009
Then, we'll be able to -- God!

822
00:36:59,044 --> 00:37:01,771
-What's the matter?
-Hard to tell.

823
00:37:01,805 --> 00:37:03,255
I think it's frequency
is so high,

824
00:37:03,290 --> 00:37:05,119
it screwed up the recorder,

825
00:37:05,153 --> 00:37:06,431
but whatever it is,
it isn't kidding.

826
00:37:06,465 --> 00:37:07,811
It's coming right at us.

827
00:37:07,846 --> 00:37:09,710
-It's headed this way.

828
00:37:09,744 --> 00:37:12,713
-Davey Johnstone.

829
00:37:12,747 --> 00:37:15,233
-What do you think? Duh.

830
00:37:15,267 --> 00:37:17,165
-How many feet away, Peter?

831
00:37:17,200 --> 00:37:19,478
-100 approximately...

832
00:37:19,513 --> 00:37:21,825
75...50...

833
00:37:21,860 --> 00:37:23,413
-See anything, Stella?

834
00:37:23,448 --> 00:37:25,657
-No, I've got nothing
on the surface.

835
00:37:25,691 --> 00:37:28,522
-It's not possible!
Keep looking.

836
00:37:28,556 --> 00:37:32,353
-25 feet,
and it's picking up speed.

837
00:37:32,388 --> 00:37:37,600
10 feet, 8 feet.
It's not a shark.

838
00:37:37,634 --> 00:37:40,154
-How would you know,
electrician?

839
00:37:40,188 --> 00:37:41,638
-I'll bet it's not a shark.

840
00:37:41,673 --> 00:37:44,089
-You are such an electrician.

841
00:37:44,123 --> 00:37:46,091
[Dolphins squeaking]

842
00:37:46,125 --> 00:37:50,716
-Dolphins win the Super Bowl!
Yay!

843
00:37:50,751 --> 00:37:53,685
-20 feet now...15.

844
00:37:53,719 --> 00:37:57,378
He's -- It's turning.

845
00:37:57,413 --> 00:37:59,553
Damn it. It's going away.

846
00:37:59,587 --> 00:38:02,176
It turned.

847
00:38:02,210 --> 00:38:03,729
It's diving.

848
00:38:03,764 --> 00:38:05,317
It's going down.

849
00:38:05,352 --> 00:38:07,285
-Can you still follow him?

850
00:38:07,319 --> 00:38:10,943
-I didn't know he was
an electrician. Mm.

851
00:38:10,978 --> 00:38:14,292
-Now I'm losing him.

852
00:38:14,326 --> 00:38:19,745
-He's gone.
-Thanks a lot, electrician.

853
00:38:19,780 --> 00:38:22,230
[Tape rewinding]

854
00:38:22,265 --> 00:38:24,440
-Good morning, Mr. European.

855
00:38:24,474 --> 00:38:26,269
[Garbling]

856
00:38:26,304 --> 00:38:27,581
-Oh, I know that sound.

857
00:38:27,615 --> 00:38:29,962
It's an oil drum being dragged
across a garage floor.

858
00:38:32,482 --> 00:38:34,829
-The sound of William
Conrad's heart...

859
00:38:36,866 --> 00:38:37,970
-Well, what do you guys want?

860
00:38:38,005 --> 00:38:39,765
I got beer, beer, and --
Oh, hey, look.

861
00:38:39,800 --> 00:38:43,079
There's a beer.
-Here, you deserve it.

862
00:38:43,113 --> 00:38:44,874
-Sorry about that electrician
crack earlier.

863
00:38:44,908 --> 00:38:47,532
My father's village was attackedby electricians.

864
00:38:47,566 --> 00:38:49,982
-I've never heard anything
quite like that.

865
00:38:50,017 --> 00:38:51,329
-Right.
It might be the sound

866
00:38:51,363 --> 00:38:53,572
of a marine specimen
we don't know about,

867
00:38:53,607 --> 00:38:56,264
and it sure scares the hell
out of all the other fish.

868
00:38:56,299 --> 00:38:58,232
-[Belches]
-Is that recording good enough

869
00:38:58,266 --> 00:39:00,683
to identify the thing?

870
00:39:00,717 --> 00:39:05,239
-Maybe, but we don't have the
proper equipment, right, boss?

871
00:39:05,273 --> 00:39:07,897
-Yeah, only that pig, West,
has it at the WOI.

872
00:39:07,931 --> 00:39:09,139
-Pig?

873
00:39:09,174 --> 00:39:10,831
-The only thing he lacks is
a little humanity.

874
00:39:10,865 --> 00:39:13,281
-So, I think our viking's
all wired up.

875
00:39:16,526 --> 00:39:20,461
-"Oh, my legs got bit off."
Be quiet, you baby.

876
00:39:20,496 --> 00:39:22,808
-Will he make it, doc?

877
00:39:22,843 --> 00:39:26,881
-We can only begin to hope
once he gets out of this coma.

878
00:39:26,916 --> 00:39:29,159
I can only tell you we're
doing everything possible.

879
00:39:29,194 --> 00:39:31,438
-Sorry, we had to put him
in this closet.

880
00:39:31,472 --> 00:39:35,096
-[Gasps]
-Ooh, Charlie horse.

881
00:39:35,131 --> 00:39:40,619
-How does kissing him help?

882
00:39:40,654 --> 00:39:44,692
-Hang on. I've got to stamp
a new price on him.

883
00:39:44,727 --> 00:39:47,419
-Intel steady at 35.

884
00:39:47,454 --> 00:39:50,215
Nurse, 4 milligrams
of adrenaline, quick.

885
00:39:52,562 --> 00:39:54,322
-Come on.

886
00:39:54,357 --> 00:39:58,637
-His broadcast day is over.

887
00:39:58,672 --> 00:39:59,845
-Doctor, the adrenaline.

888
00:39:59,880 --> 00:40:01,675
-I'll squirt it
in the general area.

889
00:40:05,610 --> 00:40:08,406
-Well, at least
he seems stabilized now.

890
00:40:11,409 --> 00:40:12,720
-Oh, I see now.

891
00:40:12,755 --> 00:40:14,998
I had it set on "kill patient."

892
00:40:15,033 --> 00:40:16,448
-I'm sorry, Sheriff.

893
00:40:16,483 --> 00:40:19,624
-You can't borrow
my smoked glasses.

894
00:40:19,658 --> 00:40:21,591
-He's dead.

895
00:40:21,626 --> 00:40:22,972
His heart just gave out.

896
00:40:23,006 --> 00:40:25,699
-Well, I gave it out, actually.
-Yeah, that was fear.

897
00:40:25,733 --> 00:40:26,907
Fear stopped his heart.

898
00:40:26,941 --> 00:40:29,357
-You'd be scared, too,
if I was your doctor.

899
00:40:33,154 --> 00:40:36,468
-Behind the scenes
at "MTV Unplugged"...

900
00:40:36,503 --> 00:40:38,919
-Need a copy made, audience?

901
00:40:42,232 --> 00:40:45,166
-Ah, the scene is starting.
Pass it on.

902
00:40:45,201 --> 00:40:46,927
-Scene is starting.
Pass it on.

903
00:40:46,961 --> 00:40:49,412
-We feel sure that whatever
is making that noise

904
00:40:49,447 --> 00:40:51,656
hasn't been classified as yet.

905
00:40:51,690 --> 00:40:53,381
-A fascinating thought.

906
00:40:53,416 --> 00:40:56,074
-I hope we can count
on your collaboration.

907
00:40:56,108 --> 00:40:58,490
Your equipment is much more
up-to-date than ours.

908
00:40:58,525 --> 00:40:59,974
-We can feed the data
to our computers

909
00:41:00,009 --> 00:41:03,909
and see what they come up with.
-[Imitating "Jaws" theme]

910
00:41:03,944 --> 00:41:05,497
-There shouldn't be any problem.

911
00:41:05,532 --> 00:41:07,603
-Of course not.

912
00:41:07,637 --> 00:41:11,434
We're delighted to assist anyone
who truly loves the sea

913
00:41:11,469 --> 00:41:13,194
and its creatures the way we do.

914
00:41:13,229 --> 00:41:14,437
-Aren't we?

915
00:41:14,472 --> 00:41:16,681
-Besides,
the possible discovery

916
00:41:16,715 --> 00:41:19,511
of a hitherto
unknown marine species

917
00:41:19,546 --> 00:41:23,411
would be of historical
importance to all of us.

918
00:41:23,446 --> 00:41:24,930
-Cookies are ready.

919
00:41:24,965 --> 00:41:28,589
-You'll have to leave usthe recorded sounds, I'm afraid.

920
00:41:28,624 --> 00:41:30,349
-How much time do you
think you'll need?

921
00:41:30,384 --> 00:41:32,835
-However long it takes.

922
00:41:32,869 --> 00:41:35,562
-Hey, did you see that?
That guy just bench pressed me.

923
00:41:35,596 --> 00:41:38,841
♪♪

924
00:41:38,875 --> 00:41:40,705
-Beery guy's theme.

925
00:41:40,739 --> 00:41:46,400
♪♪

926
00:41:46,434 --> 00:41:47,608
-Okay, what is it now?

927
00:41:47,643 --> 00:41:51,509
10, 10, 10, 10, 3, 2, 1, 10...

928
00:41:51,543 --> 00:41:54,719
-Hello,
Paleontological Institute.

929
00:41:54,753 --> 00:41:58,067
I'd like to speak
to Mrs. Bates, please.

930
00:41:58,101 --> 00:41:59,240
Janet Bates.

931
00:41:59,275 --> 00:42:01,449
-Meanwhile, in
the world today...

932
00:42:01,484 --> 00:42:03,106
[Beeping]

933
00:42:03,141 --> 00:42:05,833
-Joan Baez fan, hello.

934
00:42:05,868 --> 00:42:07,283
-Hello.
-Hello, sweetheart.

935
00:42:07,317 --> 00:42:09,630
-Oh, Bob.
-Let me finish.

936
00:42:09,665 --> 00:42:11,045
-How nice to her
your voice, again.

937
00:42:11,080 --> 00:42:12,840
Are you still
entertaining dolphins?

938
00:42:12,875 --> 00:42:14,566
-I'm calling for something
very important.

939
00:42:14,601 --> 00:42:16,119
Catch the first plane
and come down.

940
00:42:16,154 --> 00:42:18,087
-Explain why.
What's up?

941
00:42:18,121 --> 00:42:19,985
-Well, as yet,
I'm not too sure.

942
00:42:20,020 --> 00:42:22,229
Bring all your notes
on protosharks.

943
00:42:22,263 --> 00:42:23,679
-You're kidding.

944
00:42:23,713 --> 00:42:27,406
-I may be on to something
really incredible.

945
00:42:27,441 --> 00:42:29,581
♪♪

946
00:42:29,616 --> 00:42:31,859
-[Yawns]

947
00:42:31,894 --> 00:42:35,829
I'm just so tired.

948
00:42:35,863 --> 00:42:39,004
-Approximately 320 years ago,

949
00:42:39,039 --> 00:42:42,318
new forms of fish developed,
fish with teeth,

950
00:42:42,352 --> 00:42:44,527
and among them
was the Dinichthys,

951
00:42:44,562 --> 00:42:47,599
a deadly predatorthat measured over 20 feet long.

952
00:42:47,634 --> 00:42:49,394
-[Clears throat]
-[Coughing]

953
00:42:49,428 --> 00:42:51,361
-The Kronosaurus descended
from this species

954
00:42:51,396 --> 00:42:53,467
and thrived
in the Jurassic period.

955
00:42:53,501 --> 00:42:55,055
Slide, please.
-♪ Ahhh

956
00:42:55,089 --> 00:42:58,368
-This is the Tylosaurus,
another awesome predator.

957
00:42:58,403 --> 00:43:01,164
It appeared at the beginning
of the Cretaceous Period

958
00:43:01,199 --> 00:43:04,167
about 120 million years ago.

959
00:43:04,202 --> 00:43:07,101
-All: Boring!
-We consider the true ancestor

960
00:43:07,136 --> 00:43:11,658
of the shark as we know it todaywas the pseudogavious vulta,

961
00:43:11,692 --> 00:43:14,971
and it appeared at the end
of the Cretaceous Era

962
00:43:15,006 --> 00:43:17,560
60 million years ago.

963
00:43:17,595 --> 00:43:20,736
-Thanks, Kotter's wife.
-Now, then, I studied

964
00:43:20,770 --> 00:43:22,807
this cast very carefully,

965
00:43:22,841 --> 00:43:24,981
and I fed the results
of my examination

966
00:43:25,016 --> 00:43:27,294
into the computer,
then applied my knowledge...

967
00:43:27,328 --> 00:43:28,157
-Did she just got here
last night?

968
00:43:28,191 --> 00:43:31,125
-Duh...wha?

969
00:43:31,160 --> 00:43:34,439
-Now, the comparative results
are not absolutely definitive,

970
00:43:34,473 --> 00:43:37,062
but I think I can safely say...

971
00:43:37,097 --> 00:43:39,064
-[Imitates music]
-...that the creature found

972
00:43:39,099 --> 00:43:43,103
in your part of the ocean
is a living fossil.

973
00:43:49,281 --> 00:43:51,801
-And that was the day
I met Dick Meeker.

974
00:43:51,836 --> 00:43:53,527
-Aw.
-Aw. That's nice.

975
00:43:53,561 --> 00:43:56,634
-You guys, we got a call
from this weird lady --

976
00:43:56,668 --> 00:44:00,568
real mean but kind of stupid,
a lot of dishwater blond hair.

977
00:44:00,603 --> 00:44:02,536
-Oh, Mrs. Forrester.
-That's who it was.

978
00:44:02,570 --> 00:44:04,055
-Yeah.
-Anyway, she's going to be

979
00:44:04,089 --> 00:44:06,782
sending an electrician up here
to do so some stuff.

980
00:44:06,816 --> 00:44:08,335
-Thanks, Gyps.
-Okay.

981
00:44:08,369 --> 00:44:11,925
-Hey, hey, an electrician.
-So?

982
00:44:11,959 --> 00:44:14,686
-Come on. Everybody knows
about electricians.

983
00:44:14,721 --> 00:44:17,033
-Mike, just because the movie
vaguely implies

984
00:44:17,068 --> 00:44:19,553
that some electricians
may be lacking in something...

985
00:44:19,587 --> 00:44:20,830
-Are you Mike?

986
00:44:20,865 --> 00:44:23,384
I'm going to be installing
some grounded outlets

987
00:44:23,419 --> 00:44:24,731
along the baseboard
back there, so...

988
00:44:24,765 --> 00:44:26,215
-Oh, okay.Great, we need those, so thanks.

989
00:44:26,249 --> 00:44:27,699
I appreciate it.
-Oh, Mike.

990
00:44:27,734 --> 00:44:29,701
-Yeah. So, anyway,
you should be able

991
00:44:29,736 --> 00:44:31,703
to run your dehumidifier
off, as well.

992
00:44:31,738 --> 00:44:33,463
-Oh, great. You know what?
I just want to warn you,

993
00:44:33,498 --> 00:44:35,224
you've got a little spot
right there on your shirt.

994
00:44:35,258 --> 00:44:36,432
